  "discussion": "A small northwest swell will continue falling through the morning, followed by a couple of much larger swells this week. A large northwest swell will increase surf along north- and west-facing shores above High Surf Advisory thresholds tomorrow into Wednesday. Then an extra large northwest swell will fill in late Wednesday through Thanksgiving Day, boosting surf to High Surf Warning heights. Strong northerly winds behind a cold front are expected to arrive around the same time as this extra large swell, leading to rough sea conditions. This swell will shift more northerly as it subsides Friday through Saturday. Weaker trades the next few days will result in a reprieve from recent rough conditions along eastern shores with a more tranquil sea state forecast through tomorrow. Fresh to strong northerly winds and a north swell wrap will likely impact eastern shores Thanksgiving Day and Friday. Other than a very small bump in south swell expected from mid week on, there is no significant south energy expected the next several days.",
